<speak>I still go in, but not every morning. At home I can finish a piece of paperwork without hearing my name from across the room. At the office, though, I hear the little things that help me stay connected with the staff. Somebody has a child starting school, somebody is caring for an elderly parent, somebody has found a new lunch stall. I do not want to disappear completely. I just want my presence to stop meaning that every question must come to me.</speak>